# No takebacks

**Nothing grants a reroll or cancels a landed die.** Not an item, not a skill,
not a trinket, not a difficulty setting (LAWS.md #dice).

Dice land and stand. The only post-roll play is a limited-use **skill**, spent
after seeing the result, or **flee** — both of which are decisions made with
the outcome visible, not erasures of it (GAME.md #skills, #combat).

That is the whole agency layer, and it only works if the die is final. A reroll
turns every roll into a resource check and every tense moment into arithmetic.

Lint: effect-vocabulary scan. A content card offering a reroll does not merge.
